module Main exposing (main)

-- A minimal Iced counter, mapped onto Ipê's TEA over the REAL crates.io `iced`
-- crate (auto-FFI-bound, shim-free). Iced's Elm architecture is Ipê's:
--
--   Model   = a `Counter` struct  → [[rust.define.struct]]
--   Message = an `Increment`/`Decrement` enum → [[rust.define.enum]]
--   update  : Message -> Counter -> Counter → [[rust.define.closure]]
--   view    : Counter -> Element Message     → [[rust.define.closure]]
--
-- The `[rust.define.*]` decls in ipe.toml define these Rust types from Ipê and
-- emit them (plus their constructors) into the generated `_bindings.rs`. That
-- emitted Rust cargo-builds against real Iced — the SEAL for the define forms.
--
-- The Ipê-side FORWARDER plumbing for define-defined TYPES is now wired: after
-- `ipe install`, the `Rust.Iced` interface admits an opaque `Counter` / `Message`
-- nominal plus a constructor forwarder for each —
--
--     type Counter
--     type Message
--     counter_new           : Int -> Counter
--     message_new_increment : Message
--     message_new_decrement : Message
--
-- so an Ipê program can CONSTRUCT the define-defined Rust types by importing
-- `Rust.Iced exposing (Counter, Message, counter_new, message_new_increment, …)`
-- and folding over them.
--
-- REMAINING GAP (filed to the FFI backlog): handing a boxed Ipê closure to Iced's
-- `run` entrypoint. The update/view arrows return the opaque `Counter` /
-- `Element<Message>`, which needs the opaque-return + boxed-closure-as-Ipê-value
-- plumbing. So the define types are now constructible from Ipê, but the driver's
-- own event loop is not yet handed our closure. See README.md for the status.
--
-- This Main stays a placeholder rather than importing `Rust.Iced`: the interface
-- module only exists after `ipe install` runs the sandboxed inspector over real
-- `iced` (network-gated), so a checked-in import of it could not be built in CI.

import Ipe.Io as Io


main =
    Io.println "iced-counter: Counter/Message define-type forwarders wired (construct from Ipê); closure->run handoff pending (see README)."
